# Project roadmap

This page summarizes direction. It is not a release schedule or compatibility promise; [Project status](/project/status/) is the public inventory of what works now.

## Shipped foundation

- `.rocci` templates lower to ordinary Roc HTML.
- Standalone server declarations cover documents, one-shot patches, data commands, and shared live streams.
- Rocdown builds static and hybrid sites with a Rust-owned catalog and a Rocci-owned visible shell.
- The CLI provides build, run, inspect, check, test, package, and island-service workflows.
- Editor registration, language servers, desktop preview, and local macOS bundling are present.

## Near-term direction

- Keep the Rocci and Rocdown language contracts small, explicit, and well diagnosed.
- Improve site authoring, generated navigation, machine-readable output, and validation without moving presentation policy into Rust.
- Expand production packaging, signing, native capabilities, and cross-platform validation only with explicit contracts.
- Continue the reserved `@island` design separately from the shipped server-rendered hybrid path.

## How to read roadmap claims

Unchecked repository roadmap items are planned, not promised. A capability is public only after code, tests, and user documentation agree. For adoption decisions, use [Project status](/project/status/) and [known limitations](/docs/status/).
